# Basilisk Collar (equip {2}) gives the equipped creature deathtouch and lifelink. Llanowar Elves, a 1/1, equipped, attacks into
# Bot2's Ornithopter (a 0/2): its one damage is lethal because of deathtouch, so the Ornithopter dies, and Bot1 gains 1 from
# lifelink. Bot1's own Ornithopter, which is not equipped, keeps only flying (a negative control), and the equip ability is
# sorcery speed (CR 702.6a) and can't target a creature Bot1 does not control, with an equip at sorcery speed as the control.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Llanowar Elves
Basilisk Collar
Ornithopter
Forest
Forest
Forest x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Basilisk Collar.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Basilisk Collar.Activate(Ability: Equip; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Basilisk Collar.Activate(Ability: Equip; Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot2)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Keywords = Deathtouch; Lifelink
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
! Bot1.Battlefield.Basilisk Collar.Activate(Ability: Equip; Ornithopter)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 21
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Damage = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Basilisk Collar.AttachedTo = Llanowar Elves
